from (values
('111.28.b.5.B',4,'A candle is 12 inches tall and burns 1.5 inches per hour. Which equation gives its height h after t hours?','["h = 12 − 1.5t", "h = 12 + 1.5t", "h = 1.5t − 12", "h = 13.5t"]'::jsonb,0,'Start at 12 and subtract 1.5 each hour.','original'),
('111.28.b.5.B',3,'In y = 5x + 8, what is the slope?','["40", "5", "13", "8"]'::jsonb,1,'The coefficient of x is the slope.','original'),
('111.28.b.5.B',3,'In y = −3x + 9, what is the y-intercept?','["−3", "6", "9", "3"]'::jsonb,2,'The constant term is the y-intercept.','original'),
('111.28.b.5.C',3,'A scatterplot''s points fall close to a straight line rising from left to right. This suggests...','["a negative linear relationship", "no relationship", "a non-linear relationship", "a positive linear relationship"]'::jsonb,3,'The points follow a rising line.','original'),
('111.28.b.5.C',3,'A scatterplot''s points are scattered with no pattern. This suggests...','["no association", "a perfect line", "a linear association", "a strong association"]'::jsonb,0,'Without a pattern, the variables are not related.','original'),
('111.28.b.5.C',4,'A scatterplot''s points form a curve like a U. This suggests...','["no association", "a non-linear association", "a negative linear association", "a linear association"]'::jsonb,1,'The points follow a curve, not a line.','original'),
('111.28.b.5.C',3,'Points that fall along a line sloping downward suggest a...','["positive linear association", "constant", "negative linear association", "non-linear association"]'::jsonb,2,'As x increases, y decreases.','original'),
('111.28.b.5.C',4,'As the hours of practice increase, test errors decrease in a straight pattern. This is a...','["positive linear association", "non-linear association", "random pattern", "negative linear association"]'::jsonb,3,'More practice goes with fewer errors in a linear way.','original'),
('111.28.b.5.D',4,'A trend line for a plant''s height is y = 2x + 5 (cm, x weeks). What is the predicted height at 10 weeks?','["25 cm", "20 cm", "12 cm", "30 cm"]'::jsonb,0,'2(10) + 5 = 25.','original'),
('111.28.b.5.D',4,'A trend line for sales is y = 3x + 20. Predict y when x = 8.','["24", "44", "60", "28"]'::jsonb,1,'3(8) + 20 = 44.','original'),
('111.28.b.5.D',3,'A trend line is used to...','["remove outliers", "avoid graphing", "predict values that are not in the data", "prove the data is exact"]'::jsonb,2,'It approximates the pattern for predictions.','original'),
('111.28.b.5.D',4,'A trend line y = −4x + 90 models temperature. Predict y when x = 5.','["110", "20", "86", "70"]'::jsonb,3,'−4(5) + 90 = 70.','original'),
('111.28.b.5.D',4,'A scatterplot shows a trend line passing through (2, 11) and (6, 23). Predict y at x = 10.','["35", "29", "46", "33"]'::jsonb,0,'The slope is 3, so from (6, 23) add 12.','original'),
('111.28.b.5.E',3,'If y varies directly with x and y = 12 when x = 3, what is the constant of variation?','["1/4", "4", "9", "36"]'::jsonb,1,'12 ÷ 3 = 4.','original'),
('111.28.b.5.E',4,'If y varies directly with x and y = 20 when x = 4, find y when x = 7.','["28", "27", "35", "11"]'::jsonb,2,'k = 5, so y = 5 × 7 = 35.','original'),
('111.28.b.5.E',4,'The cost of fabric varies directly with its length. 6 yards cost $27. How much do 10 yards cost?','["$33", "$60", "$37", "$45"]'::jsonb,3,'k = 4.5, so 10 × 4.5 = 45.','original'),
('111.28.b.5.E',3,'Which equation shows direct variation?','["y = 9x", "y = x²", "y = 9 − x", "y = 9x + 2"]'::jsonb,0,'Direct variation has the form y = kx.','original'),
('111.28.b.5.E',4,'y varies directly with x. When x = 2, y = 5. What is y when x = 12?','["60", "30", "25", "17"]'::jsonb,1,'k = 2.5, and 2.5 × 12 = 30.','original'),
('111.28.b.5.F',3,'Which equation represents a non-proportional relationship?','["y = 2x", "y = x/2", "y = 2x + 3", "y = 5x"]'::jsonb,2,'A nonzero y-intercept means it is not proportional.','original'),
('111.28.b.5.F',3,'Which table is non-proportional?','["x: 1, 2, 3 and y: 2, 4, 6", "x: 1, 2, 3 and y: 4, 8, 12", "x: 1, 2, 3 and y: 10, 20, 30", "x: 1, 2, 3 and y: 3, 5, 7"]'::jsonb,3,'y/x is 3, 2.5, 2.33, so the ratio changes.','original'),
('111.28.b.5.F',4,'A line passes through (0, 0) and (3, 9). This relationship is...','["proportional", "undefined", "non-proportional", "not linear"]'::jsonb,0,'It passes through the origin and has constant ratio 3.','original'),
('111.28.b.5.F',4,'A line passes through (0, 4) and (2, 10). This relationship is...','["not a function", "non-proportional", "proportional", "undefined"]'::jsonb,1,'The line does not pass through the origin.','original'),
('111.28.b.5.F',4,'A video plan costs $5 per month with no fee. A different plan costs $2 to join plus $4 per month. Which is proportional?','["both plans", "the second plan, y = 4x + 2", "the first plan, y = 5x", "neither plan"]'::jsonb,2,'Only y = 5x has no starting amount.','original'),
('111.28.b.5.G',3,'Which set of ordered pairs is a function?','["{(0, 0), (0, 1), (2, 2)}", "{(2, 1), (2, 3), (4, 5)}", "{(1, 2), (1, 4), (3, 6)}", "{(1, 2), (2, 4), (3, 6)}"]'::jsonb,3,'Each input has exactly one output.','original'),
('111.28.b.5.G',3,'Which set of ordered pairs is NOT a function?','["{(3, 1), (3, 5), (4, 2)}", "{(0, 2), (1, 3), (2, 4)}", "{(5, 9), (6, 8), (7, 7)}", "{(1, 1), (2, 1), (3, 1)}"]'::jsonb,0,'The input 3 has two outputs.','original'),
('111.28.b.5.G',4,'A table shows x = 2, 4, 2 and y = 5, 9, 7. Is this a function?','["No, because y values differ", "No, because x = 2 has two outputs", "Yes, because y values are different", "Yes, because x increases"]'::jsonb,1,'A function cannot give two outputs for the same input.','original'),
('111.28.b.5.G',4,'A graph fails the vertical line test when...','["it has a y-intercept", "a horizontal line touches it once", "a vertical line touches it in more than one point", "it is a straight line through the origin"]'::jsonb,2,'That means an input has more than one output.','original'),
('111.28.b.5.G',3,'A mapping sends 1→3, 2→3 and 3→3. Is it a function?','["It cannot be told", "No, inputs repeat", "No, outputs repeat", "Yes, each input has one output"]'::jsonb,3,'Repeated outputs are allowed; repeated inputs with different outputs are not.','original'),
('111.28.b.5.G',4,'Which relation is a function?','["a student ID number to that student''s name", "a grade level to all students in it", "a birthday to all students born that day", "a first name to all students with that name"]'::jsonb,0,'Each ID matches one name.','original'),
('111.28.b.5.H',3,'Which situation is proportional?','["a phone plan with a $20 base fee", "buying apples at $2 per pound", "a plant that is 10 cm tall and grows 2 cm per week", "a $5 delivery fee plus $2 per pound"]'::jsonb,1,'No starting amount means the cost is proportional to the weight.','original'),
('111.28.b.5.H',3,'Which situation is non-proportional?','["buying tickets at $8 each", "earning $12 per hour with no bonus", "a gym with a $30 sign-up fee and $15 per month", "a car at a steady 60 miles per hour from the start"]'::jsonb,2,'The sign-up fee gives a nonzero starting value.','original'),
('111.28.b.5.H',4,'Which is a non-proportional function?','["distance at a constant speed from rest", "the pay for hours at a flat hourly rate", "the cost of identical items sold at one price", "the cost of a taxi ride with a base fare"]'::jsonb,3,'A base fare gives a nonzero y-intercept.','original'),
('111.28.b.5.H',4,'The area of a square, A = s², compared with its side length is...','["non-proportional (and non-linear)", "linear and proportional", "proportional", "a direct variation"]'::jsonb,0,'Doubling s quadruples A.','original'),
('111.28.b.5.H',3,'The perimeter of a square, P = 4s, is...','["not proportional", "proportional to its side length", "quadratic", "unrelated to s"]'::jsonb,1,'P = 4s has the form y = kx.','original'),
('111.28.b.5.I',4,'A line passes through (0, 3) and (2, 7). Which is its equation?','["y = 2x + 7", "y = 4x + 3", "y = 2x + 3", "y = 3x + 2"]'::jsonb,2,'Slope 4/2 = 2 and y-intercept 3.','original'),
('111.28.b.5.I',4,'A table shows x = 0, 1, 2, 3 and y = 10, 8, 6, 4. Which equation fits?','["y = 2x + 10", "y = 10x − 2", "y = −2x − 10", "y = −2x + 10"]'::jsonb,3,'y drops by 2 each step starting at 10.','original'),
('111.28.b.5.I',4,'A phone plan costs $15 per month plus $0.10 per text. Which equation gives the cost y for x texts?','["y = 0.10x + 15", "y = 15x + 0.10", "y = 15.10x", "y = 0.10x − 15"]'::jsonb,0,'Per-text rate times texts plus the base.','original'),
('111.28.b.5.I',4,'A line with slope 3 passes through (0, −5). Which is its equation?','["y = 3x + 5", "y = 3x − 5", "y = −5x + 3", "y = −3x − 5"]'::jsonb,1,'m = 3 and b = −5.','original'),
('111.28.b.5.I',4,'A pool has 200 gallons and drains 8 gallons per minute. Which equation gives gallons g after m minutes?','["g = 8m − 200", "g = 192m", "g = 200 − 8m", "g = 200 + 8m"]'::jsonb,2,'Start at 200 and subtract 8 each minute.','original'),
('111.28.b.5.I',3,'Which equation has slope 4 and y-intercept 7?','["y = 11x", "y = 4x − 7", "y = 7x + 4", "y = 4x + 7"]'::jsonb,3,'y = mx + b.','original'),
('111.28.b.6.A',3,'The volume formula for a cylinder is V = Bh. What does B represent?','["the area of the base", "the radius", "the circumference", "the height"]'::jsonb,0,'B is the base area, which for a cylinder is πr².','original'),
('111.28.b.6.A',3,'A cylinder has a base area of 50 square centimeters and height 6 centimeters. What is its volume?','["150 cubic centimeters", "300 cubic centimeters", "56 cubic centimeters", "600 cubic centimeters"]'::jsonb,1,'V = Bh = 50 × 6.','original'),
('111.28.b.6.A',4,'Which formula gives the volume of a cylinder with radius r and height h?','["V = πrh", "V = 2πrh", "V = πr²h", "V = 1/3πr²h"]'::jsonb,2,'Base area πr² times height.','original'),
('111.28.b.6.A',4,'A cylinder has radius 3 and height 5. What is its volume in terms of π?','["15π", "75π", "30π", "45π"]'::jsonb,3,'π(3²)(5) = 45π.','original'),
('111.28.b.6.A',4,'Two cylinders have the same base. One is twice as tall. Its volume is...','["twice as large", "half as large", "four times as large", "the same"]'::jsonb,0,'V = Bh grows with h.','original'),
('111.28.b.6.B',3,'A cone and a cylinder have congruent bases and equal heights. The cone''s volume is what fraction of the cylinder''s?','["1/4", "1/3", "1/2", "2/3"]'::jsonb,1,'Three cones fill one cylinder.','original'),
('111.28.b.6.B',3,'Which is the volume formula for a cone?','["V = πr²h", "V = 4/3 πr³", "V = 1/3 πr²h", "V = 2πrh"]'::jsonb,2,'One-third of the cylinder formula.','original'),
('111.28.b.6.B',4,'A cylinder holds 90 cubic inches. A cone has the same base and height. How many cubic inches does the cone hold?','["45", "270", "60", "30"]'::jsonb,3,'90 ÷ 3 = 30.','original'),
('111.28.b.6.B',4,'How many full cones of water fill an empty cylinder with the same base and height?','["3", "4", "2", "6"]'::jsonb,0,'V(cone) = 1/3 V(cylinder).','original'),
('111.28.b.6.B',4,'A cone has volume 24π. A cylinder has the same base and height. What is the cylinder''s volume?','["24π", "72π", "48π", "8π"]'::jsonb,1,'24π × 3 = 72π.','original')
